  ('mahahual-mexico', '10S', 'Mahahual (Costa Maya & Banco Chinchorro)', 'Mexico', 'The largest coral atoll in the Northern Hemisphere', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"liveaboard","diveglobal"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Banco Chinchorro - largest coral atoll in the Northern Hemisphere; biosphere 144,000 ha; ~25x10 mi","~80-90 min (some ops ~2.5h) boat from Mahahual; ~200 shipwrecks; permit-restricted (op handles permit)","Best viz May-Sep (~15-30m); crocodile-encounter season Jun 1-Sep 30 (XTC = sole federal permit)","Overnight = palafito stilt-hut on Cayo Centro (legalized 2010; no services) - the liveaboard-style product","Costa Maya cruise port (2nd-largest in Caribbean Mexico, up to ~20k cruisers) = OUT of TWW cruise scope"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","dan_emergency":"+1-919-684-9111","advisory_level":"L2","nearest_chamber":"Costamed, COZUMEL (DAN-certified) - Mahahual clinic has NO chamber; long medevac from Chinchorro","nearest_trauma":"Chetumal (Hospital General, south) or evac to Cancun","malaria":"NONE in tourist zone; dengue present","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"Jun-Nov, peak Aug-Oct","dive_no_fly":"18-24h (DAN)","special_rule":"REMOTE-MEDEVAC - dive conservative; permitted+certified op only; croc encounter handler-led, max 6/trip","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dive peak May-Sep (viz ~15-30m; croc encounter hard window Jun 1-Sep 30)","shoulder":"Apr and Oct edges","green":"Nov-Mar (wind/swell; Chinchorro often blown out - fall back to Costa Maya/Xcalak reef)","booking_lead":"4-6 months for permit-limited summer Chinchorro/croc product (permit scarcity = longer lead than a general reef trip)","off_season_specials":"winter Nov-Mar: Costa Maya/Xcalak mainland-reef dive days + no-fly beach fill-the-beds (lean Xcalak, south of the cruise port)","event_peaks":"croc window Jun 1-Sep 30; (Costa Maya cruise day-crowds peak Sep-Dec, busiest Nov, Wed/Thu - OUT of TWW scope, plan dive departures around it)","campaign_start":"live by Dec-Jan, ~4-6 months ahead of the May-Sep dive window; run a winter Xcalak-reef value campaign for Nov-Mar fill-the-beds"},"jewels":[{"name":"Chinchorro overnight palafito expedition (Cayo Centro)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"live","bookable_category":"multi-day dive expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://pepedivemahahual.com/en/diving/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"multi-day dive with stilt-hut overnight on the atoll ·","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"multi-day dive with stilt-hut overnight on the atoll ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"on application (liveaboard-reseller/dive-op host)"},{"name":"~200-wreck atoll dives","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards","status":"live","bookable_category":"wreck/wall diving","tier":"premier","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host ~10-20% / on application"},{"name":"Chinchorro day-boat 2-3 tank + Cayo Centro","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"live","bookable_category":"day dive charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/chinchorro/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"state day-trip, 2-tank $275 / 3-tank $325, Cayo Centro surface stop ·","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"state day-trip, 2-tank $275 / 3-tank $325, Cayo Centro surface stop ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host / affiliate"},{"name":"Costa Maya / Xcalak reef diving","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"live","bookable_category":"day dive charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://amigosdelmar.net/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host ~10-20%"},{"name":"Wild American-crocodile in-water encounter (XTC)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","bookable_category":"expert-guided wildlife","tier":"premier","source":"https://xtcdivecenter.com/crocs/croc-encounters/","timing":"Dive peak May-Sep","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"handler-led encounter, world''s only permitted such experience ·","si":"expedition","blurb":"handler-led encounter, world''s only permitted such experience ·","when":"Dive peak May-Sep","commission":"dive-op host / on application; XTC sole permit"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for diving Mahahual?","a":"Remote medevac - the load-bearing risk. Mahahual has NO hyperbaric chamber; the nearest DAN-certified chamber is in Cozumel, a multi-hour transit from a Chinchorro site ~25 miles offshore. Dive conservatively, hold no-fly 18-24h, and treat DCS as a logistics problem.","source":"costamed.com.mx","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Mahahual and Chinchorro?","a":"May-September - the counterintuitive answer: calmest seas, best visibility (~15-30m) and the crocodile season (Jun 1-Sep 30), even though it overlaps the rainy/hurricane months. Winter (Nov-Mar) sees more wind and Chinchorro is often blown out.","source":"coralrealm.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I day-dive Banco Chinchorro, and how?","a":"Yes - most Mahahual/Xcalak operators run day-trips for certified divers: a 2-tank ($275) or 3-tank ($325) day with a Cayo Centro stop, an 80-90-minute crossing each way. The operator handles the limited federal permit when you book; May-September has the calmest seas.","source":"xtcdivecenter.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can you really swim with wild crocodiles at Chinchorro?","a":"Yes - it''s the only legally permitted in-water wild-crocodile encounter on Earth, and only XTC Dive Center holds the federal permit. The season is a hard window of June 1 to September 30, capped at 6 people (2 in the water with the handler at a time), flotation device required. Book far ahead.","source":"xtcdivecenter.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What is the Banco Chinchorro liveaboard experience actually like?","a":"It''s a stilt-hut expedition, not a cruise ship. Multi-day trips overnight in a palafito on Cayo Centro - a basic 2x2m stilt-deck fishing hut with hammocks and no services - legalized in 2010. It''s the closest access to the remote walls and ~200 wrecks; permit-scarce, so book the specialist operator well ahead.","source":"pepedivemahahual.com","si_tag":"liveaboard"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mahahual & Banco Chinchorro: Atoll Diving Guide","meta_description":"Mahahual is the gateway to Banco Chinchorro - the Northern Hemisphere''s largest coral atoll: ~200 wrecks, croc encounters, and the remote-chamber realities.","slug":"mahahual-mexico","primary_keyword":"Banco Chinchorro diving","long_tail":["Mahahual Banco Chinchorro dive","Chinchorro liveaboard palafito","Chinchorro crocodile snorkel XTC","Costa Maya diving","Xcalak scuba diving"],"search_language":"es","local_keywords":["buceo Banco Chinchorro","Mahahual buceo Costa Maya","encuentro con cocodrilos Xcalak","buceo Xcalak","atolon Chinchorro liveaboard palafito"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"note":"Quintana Roo US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution, dated 2026-05-29) - freely bookable; the real planning is dive-medevac (nearest chamber Cozumel), not crime; MXN currency, dive prices often USD-quoted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-30","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; Banco Chinchorro moat = largest N-Hemisphere atoll (~200 wrecks) + sole permitted wild-crocodile encounter (XTC); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","name":"liveaboard","status":"live","note":"overnight-palafito multi-day on Cayo Centro (stilt-hut, not a cruise ship)"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private crewed Chinchorro dive charter / private palafito buy-out","why_ultra":"exclusive-use permitted multi-day atoll expedition - the rarest dive product in Mexican waters (permit-scarce, ~200 wrecks, sole-group access)","earning":"on application (dive-op/charter host / liveaboard-reseller)","virtuoso_value_add":"none formal (specialist dive charter, not a consortia hotel)","mor":"commission-on-net, agent-of-record; no net-rate resale"},{"name":"Nearest branded ultra = Riviera Maya (Mayakoba: Rosewood/Banyan Tree; Maroma A Belmond)","why_ultra":"n/a locally - branded-residence ultra sits far north; route ultra client Mahahual-for-dive + Riviera-Maya-for-stay","earning":"via host-Virtuoso (see Playa del Carmen / Puerto Morelos dossiers)","virtuoso_value_add":"upgrade / breakfast / resort credit (per those dossiers)","mor":"commission-on-net"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Mahahual (Costa Maya & Banco Chinchorro), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":18.7167,"lng":-87.7167}}'::jsonb, 62),
