mier","source":"https://www.rainforestcruises.com/cruises/iberostar-grand-amazon","hook":"72-cabin 5★ all-inclusive expedition boat, 4/5/8-day Solimões + Negro itineraries from Manaus, English-guided excursions, ending at the Meeting of the Waters","si":"river","blurb":"72-cabin 5★ all-inclusive expedition boat, 4/5/8-day Solimões + Negro itineraries from Manaus, English-guided excursions, ending at the Meeting of the Waters","commission":"DMC / consortia / cruise affiliate; all-inclusive package"},{"name":"Small-group expedition riverboat (Katerre / Jacaré-Açu)","si_tag":"river","tier":"premier","source":"https://amazonastravel.com.br/expedicao-katerre-i.html","hook":"low-impact small-group boats, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas / Jaú, full board with drinks, bilingual guide, park entries, Novo Airão embarkation","si":"river","blurb":"low-impact small-group boats, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas / Jaú, full board with drinks, bilingual guide, park entries, Novo Airão embarkation","commission":"DMC / operator (Amazonas by Viverde) net/commission package"},{"name":"Anavilhanas archipelago","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://national-parks.org/brazil/anavilhanas-national-park/","hook":"the second-largest river archipelago on Earth: 400 forested islands over 90 km of the Rio Negro, a UNESCO-caliber protected area of igarapés, black-water channels","si":"wildlife","blurb":"the second-largest river archipelago on Earth: 400 forested islands over 90 km of the Rio Negro, a UNESCO-caliber protected area of igarapés, black-water channels","commission":"DMC / lodge / riverboat; park fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Pink river dolphins (boto), Novo Airão","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/swimming-with-pink-dolphins-in-brazil/","hook":"the famous Rio Negro boto, encountered at regulated floating platforms ~180 km from Manaus; a genuine wildlife highlight","si":"wildlife","blurb":"the famous Rio Negro boto, encountered at regulated floating platforms ~180 km from Manaus; a genuine wildlife highlight","commission":"DMC day-trip / lodge excursion; platform-regulated"},{"name":"Indigenous / ribeirinho community visit","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://amazontourmanaus.com/manaus-amazon/the-amazon-rainforest/anavilhanas-national-park/item162","hook":"a visit to a river-people or indigenous community, done through a genuinely vetted, community-consenting operator","si":"wildlife","blurb":"a visit to a river-people or indigenous community, done through a genuinely vetted, community-consenting operator","commission":"vetted DMC / operator AOR only (ethical, community-consenting)"},{"name":"Teatro Amazonas opera house","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons / Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Theatre","hook":"the 1896 belle-époque jewel of the rubber boom: Alsatian roof tiles, Glaswegian steel, Carrara-marble stairs, a dome of 36,000 tiles in the national colours","si":"Romance & Honeymoons / Culture","blurb":"the 1896 belle-époque jewel of the rubber boom: Alsatian roof tiles, Glaswegian steel, Carrara-marble stairs, a dome of 36,000 tiles in the national colours","commission":"DMC / city-tour affiliate; performance/visit ticket non-commissionable"},{"name":"Design jungle-lodge honeymoon (Mirante do Gavião / Anavilhanas)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.here-away.com/mirantedogaviaoamazonlodge","hook":"a boutique design lodge over black water: canopy hammock, private dawn canoe, floating bar, spa/wellness space, dolphin-swim afternoon. The adventurous honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"a boutique design lodge over black water: canopy hammock, private dawn canoe, floating bar, spa/wellness space, dolphin-swim afternoon. The adventurous honeymoon","commission":"DMC lodge package / consortia (AOR)"}],"faq":null,"seo":{"meta_title":"Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon Travel Guide 2026 — Meeting of the Waters, Jungle Lodges & Amazon Cruises | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Manaus Amazônia o que fazer","Encontro das Águas passeio","cruzeiro Rio Negro Amazonas","melhores lodges de selva na Amazônia","botos cor-de-rosa Novo Airão","cachoeiras Presidente Figueiredo","Teatro Amazonas visita","vacina febre amarela Manaus","Manaus é seguro para turistas","lua de mel na Amazônia","arquipélago de Anavilhanas","Amazônia cheia e vazante melhor época"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Mirante do Gavião Amazon Lodge","lane":"Fora/consortia","mor":"consortia","tier":"ultra","note":"12-suite design lodge, Novo Airão / Anavilhanas edge"},{"name":"Anavilhanas Jungle Lodge","lane":"consortia/Fora","mor":"consortia","tier":"premier","note":"glass-wall bungalows, floating bar, pool, spa"},{"name":"Juma Amazon Lodge","lane":"consortia/DMC","mor":"consortia/DMC","tier":"comfort","note":"stilted treetop bungalows ~15m, solar-powered"},{"name":"Iberostar Grand Amazon (riverboat)","lane":"consortia/cruise affiliate","mor":"consortia/operator","tier":"premier","note":"72-cabin all-inclusive expedition; verify consortia lane"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Manaus & the Brazilian Amazon, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-3.119,"lng":-60.0217}}'::jsonb, 63),
  ('manuel-antonio-costa-rica', '10S', 'Manuel Antonio', 'Costa Rica', 'Sloths, monkeys and Pacific cliffs', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Costa Rica', '{"tropical","expedition","wildlife"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Manuel Antonio NP is open Wed–Mon 07:00–16:00, CLOSED every Tuesday; adult entry US$18, child (2–12) US$5, under-2 free; advance online ticket + passport number required.","One of few places to see all of Costa Rica''s iconic wildlife at a beach: 2- & 3-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (90%+ of visits), endangered Central American squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans.","Two park beaches: crescent Playa Manuel Antonio (calm, turquoise — the calmest, patrolled swim) and longer, choppier Playa Espadilla Sur.","Access: ~2.5–3 hr / ~168 km drive from San José (SJO), OR ~25-min domestic flight to Quepos–Manuel Antonio (XQP) on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways + 15 km / 25-min transfer.","Cliffside-resort belt (Arenas del Mar, Makanda, Gaia, Tulemar) makes it a top romance/honeymoon hub; hillside villas make it a strong family/multi-gen hub."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital Metropolitano Quepos (private, 24-hr, marina) + public Max Terán Valls Hospital; serious cases to San José major hospitals (~2.5–3 hr) with air evac available","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"l2_disclosure":true,"advisory_note":"US Level 2 Exercise Increased Caution (reissued 2026-04-02); clean L2, no L4 zone near Manuel Antonio/Quepos; standard caution — petty crime, don''t display wealth, avoid poorly lit beaches at night, enroll in STEP","air_access_verified":"SJO gateway; XQP (Quepos–Manuel Antonio) ~25-min domestic flight on Sansa / Costa Rica Green Airways, or ~2.5–3 hr drive from SJO","riptide":"HARD FLAG — rip currents are the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (>80% of drownings); most beaches unguarded. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches (the park cove is the calmest and patrolled), heed red flags, never swim alone; if caught, swim parallel to shore.","wildlife":"Bold habituated monkeys/raccoons/coatis raid food — no feeding, seal food, don''t leave bags unattended","dengue":"Year-round mosquito-borne risk (higher green season May–Nov); no widely available traveler vaccine — DEET/picaridin, cover at dawn/dusk, screened/AC rooms","water":"Tap water in San José & major tourist areas (incl. Manuel Antonio/Quepos) treated and generally safe; sensitive stomachs / remote lodges use bottled/filtered","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late October–early November","peak":"mid-December–April (Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa ~1 yr lead)","fire_date":"2026-10-17","shoulder":"May–November (green-season value)","green":"May–November (afternoon rain; lush, lower rates)","booking_lead":"3–8 weeks normal peak; ~1 year for Christmas/New Year & Semana Santa (lead pressure on cliffside-resort + villa beds)","off_season_specials":"green-season resort/villa discounts + whale-watching backfill (Jul–Oct/Nov Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks)","event_peaks":["Whale season Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep)","Whale season Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb)","Christmas/New Year","Semana Santa (Easter)"],"operational_note":"Manuel Antonio NP closed every Tuesday — route park visit Wed–Mon; slot waterfalls/catamaran/mangrove on Tuesday"},"jewels":[{"name":"Playa Manuel Antonio (in-park)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Crescent white sand + calm turquoise — the park''s calmest, patrolled swim and best snorkel, backed by monkey-filled rainforest.","bookable_category":"guided park tour / DIY ticket","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mustseespots.com/costa-rica/articles/manuel-antonio-national-park-beaches-wildlife-trails-explained/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","blurb":"Crescent white sand + calm turquoise — the park''s calmest, patrolled swim and best snorkel, backed by monkey-filled rainforest.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"GYG/Viator or host-IATA guide; park entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Playa Biesanz","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Small jungle-backed calm cove on Quepos Point — the local''s-choice calm-swim/kayak/snorkel beach away from crowds.","bookable_category":"DIY + gear / guided kayak-snorkel","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","blurb":"Small jungle-backed calm cove on Quepos Point — the local''s-choice calm-swim/kayak/snorkel beach away from crowds.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"thin/DIY concierge add-on; small guided kayak-snorkel via affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Catamaran sunset + snorkel","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~4-hr coastal catamaran with snorkeling, meals, seasonal dolphins/whales — the signature on-the-water romance experience.","bookable_category":"catamaran tour / private charter","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/Snorkeling_Tours.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~4-hr coastal catamaran with snorkeling, meals, seasonal dolphins/whales — the signature on-the-water romance experience.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; DMC/host-IATA for private charter","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~1.5 hr away; steep hike (or 4x4/horseback) to two massive cascades + natural swimming pools.","bookable_category":"guided day tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1.5 hr away; steep hike (or 4x4/horseback) to two massive cascades + natural swimming pools.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Damas Island mangrove kayak","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","bookable_category":"half-day kayak tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/manuel-antonio/tours/Half-Day-Kayak-Damas-Mangroves.php + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"Calm-water estuary/mangrove kayak north of Quepos — monkeys, crocodiles and birds; superb family + wildlife half-day.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + local operator; host-IATA private","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Rainmaker canopy + hanging bridges","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","bookable_category":"guided canopy/bridges tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.earthtrekkers.com/things-to-do-in-manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"~1,400-acre private rainforest reserve with waterfalls, trails and Mistico-style suspension bridges — lower-crowd canopy near Manuel Antonio.","when":"year-round","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate; host-IATA land services","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Quepos marina sportfishing","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","bookable_category":"charter","tier":"premier","source":"https://costaricaexperts.com/destinations/manuel-antonio/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Marina Pez Vela — top Pacific billfish/sailfish + dorado sportfishing base; premier half/full-day charters.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"host-IATA / private-charter agent-of-record; premium day rates","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Whale-watching (Marino Ballena / Uvita)","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","bookable_category":"guided whale-watching boat tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://puravidamoms.com/whale-watching-uvita-tour-guide/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"expedition","blurb":"~45–60 min south; two humpback seasons (Jul–Oct/Nov + Dec–Mar/Apr) at the whale''s-tail sandbar — spans both green & dry season.","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate + host-IATA; Marino Ballena entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"National Park wildlife walk (sloths + 4 monkey species)","si_tag":"Wildlife","status":"future","hook":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","bookable_category":"guided park wildlife tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.adventuretourscostarica.com/blog/spotting-sloths-monkeys-your-manuel-antonio-wildlife-guide + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"mid-December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"2- & 3-toed sloths, capuchins, endangered squirrel monkeys, howlers, coatis, toucans — reliably seen with a certified scope-guide.","when":"mid-December–April","commission":"GYG/Viator affiliate or host-IATA guide; park entry non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio National Park open on Tuesday?","a":"No — the park is closed every Tuesday, year-round including holidays. It is open Wednesday–Monday 07:00–16:00; adult entry is $18, children 2–12 $5, under-2 free, and advance online ticket purchase with your passport number is required — route the park visit Wed–Mon.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can you see whales near Manuel Antonio?","a":"Yes — nearby Marino Ballena / Uvita has two humpback seasons. Southern-Hemisphere humpbacks run Jul–Oct/Nov (peak Aug–Sep) and Northern-Hemisphere humpbacks Dec–Mar/Apr (peak Jan–Feb), a rare draw spanning both the green and dry seasons, ~45–60 min south by guided boat tour.","source":"puravidamoms.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Manuel Antonio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — it''s one of Costa Rica''s premier romance hubs. The cliffside-resort belt above the beach, led by adults-only Makanda by the Sea ~100 m above the ocean, defines the honeymoon identity, while Arenas del Mar is the only true beachfront luxury resort with two private beaches.","source":"oyster.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you really see sloths and monkeys at the beach?","a":"Yes — it''s one of very few places anywhere you reliably can. Two- and three-toed sloths, white-faced capuchins (on 90%+ of visits), the endangered Central American squirrel monkey, howlers, coatis and toucans all live inside a compact, walkable national park where the rainforest meets the sand.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife-—-future"},{"q":"What''s the biggest safety risk in Manuel Antonio?","a":"Pacific rip currents — the leading cause of tourist drowning in Costa Rica (over 80% of drownings), on mostly unguarded beaches. Swim only at guarded/flagged beaches — the guarded park cove of Playa Manuel Antonio is the calmest water and the only patrolled swim — heed red flags, never swim alone, and if caught, swim parallel to shore.","source":"crie.cr, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the monkeys a problem in the park?","a":"They can be — capuchins, raccoons and coatis are bold and habituated and will raid open bags and grab food. Don''t feed wildlife, keep food sealed and bags zipped, and don''t leave belongings unattended on the beach.","source":"adventuretourscostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica Travel Guide — Sloths, Rainforest Beaches, Cliffside Resorts & Quepos | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"See sloths and monkeys at a Pacific beach, base on the Quepos cliffs for romance or in a villa for family, and do Manuel Antonio well, safely, and at the right time — park hours, riptide safety, whales, catamarans and waterfalls.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","long_tail_en":["Manuel Antonio National Park hours 2026","is Manuel Antonio open on Tuesday","best time to visit Manuel Antonio Costa Rica","Manuel Antonio sloths and monkeys guide","Manuel Antonio riptide beach safety","SJO to Quepos flight Manuel Antonio","Manuel Antonio cliffside honeymoon resorts","Manuel Antonio villas with pool family","Nauyaca Waterfalls day trip from Manuel Antonio","Uvita whale watching season from Manuel Antonio"],"local_keywords":["Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio","playas Manuel Antonio","qué hacer en Quepos","avistamiento de ballenas Uvita Marino Ballena","cataratas Nauyaca desde Manuel Antonio","kayak manglares isla Damas","perezosos y monos Manuel Antonio","hoteles de lujo Manuel Antonio","vuelo San José a Quepos","horario Parque Nacional Manuel Antonio precio entrada"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Arenas del Mar (Böÿ Collection / Cayuga)","why_ultra":"The only true beachfront luxury resort in Manuel Antonio — private ridge, two secluded beaches (golf-cart access), rainforest all around, strong sustainability, ocean-view suites with plunge pools. The apex property.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity block; agent-of-record commission","consortia_value_add":"upgrade, breakfast/resort credit, early/late, VIP welcome (confirm current program)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record","tier":"luxury / ultra"},{"name":"Makanda by the Sea","why_ultra":"Adults-only (16+), ~100 m above the ocean on 12 acres of rainforest gardens — the definitive Manuel Antonio honeymoon/romance property; small, private, view-forward.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + amenity","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit where program allows (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Gaia Hotel & Reserve","why_ultra":"Eco-chic adults-oriented 22-room private-reserve hillside hotel; 500-thread-count linens, wellness + service focus.","earning":"consortia/agent rate","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA","tier":"premier / luxury"},{"name":"Tulemar Resort (+ private villas)","why_ultra":"Gated hillside estate with its own private sandy beach, 4 pools, concierge, spa, and a portfolio of private villas — the best resort-serviced villa play for families/multi-gen.","earning":"consortia/agent rate + villa MoR","consortia_value_add":"upgrade/credit + villa perks (verify)","mor":"Fora / host-IATA agent-of-record + villa direct-contract","tier":"premier / luxury (villas: luxury/ultra)"},{"name":"Preferred / luxury hillside villas","why_ultra":"Private ocean-view villas (chef/staff, pools, 2–8 br) — the whole-property-buyout ultra lane for honeymooners + multi-gen groups.","earning":"villa MoR + agent-of-record","consortia_value_add":"n/a (villa direct-contract perks vary)","mor":"direct-contract / villa specialist (host-IATA)","tier":"luxury / ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.392,"lng":-84.137}}'::jsonb, 64),
  ('mazamitla-mexico', '10S', 'Mazamitla', 'Mexico', 'Chalet cabañas in a pine-oak Sierra', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"expedition","family","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Pueblo Mágico (2005) at ~2,200 m in southern Jalisco, ~124–135 km / ~2 hr from Guadalajara; ''Switzerland of Mexico'' (Source: travelagewest.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Cool year-round (~15°C avg; ~7–26°C) — a magnet for Guadalajara residents, esp. summer (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazamitla, Accessed 2026-07-04)","El Salto waterfall ~35 m in Los Cazos (private, ~US$1, ~45-min forest hike or horse ~M$250) (Source: zonaturistica.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Signature chalet cabañas (e.g., Cabañas Monteverde: kitchens, fireplaces, daily firewood) (Source: travelagewest.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Canopy/zipline + six-hanging-bridge tours (Green Forest Tours); La Zanja 1977 town forest (Source: theguadalajarapost.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"No major trauma hospital in town; nearest full ER/trauma is Guadalajara ~2 hr / ~124–135 km back down mountain road; local clinic for minor cases; air-evac to US for critical cases","advisory_level":"L3","book_enabled":false,"tourist_zone_carveout":"none","air_access_verified":"via GDL ~2 hr ground (not into a carve-out); approach via Hwy 405 (advisory-designated route)","advisory_note":"Advisory names Mazamitla as a specific EXCEPTION to the Hwy-110 restriction and directs ''travel via Highway 405 only'' — stronger than a blanket exclusion, but still NOT a named safe-zone carve-out; ruling holds at no-Book","malaria":"none","dengue":"very low at ~2,200 m (above Aedes aegypti elevation ceiling)","yellow_fever":"not required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Domestic-holiday & weekend peaks — summer (GDL heat escape) + Semana Santa + Christmas/New-Year + long weekends; cool ~15°C year-round draw","waterfall_flow_peak":"October–December (fullest El Salto flow, post-rains)","shoulder":"Non-holiday weekdays / shoulder months","green":"Deep off-holiday midweeks (softest domestic demand)","booking_lead":"Weeks–months for Semana Santa/summer/Christmas/long-weekend cabañas; midweek walk-up-easy; largely direct/domestic","event_peaks":"Semana Santa, summer school holidays, Christmas–New-Year, Mexican puentes","campaign_start":"''Cool-mountain weekend from Guadalajara'' ahead of summer + Semana Santa; waterfall-flow (Oct–Dec) into fall"},"jewels":[{"name":"El Salto waterfall (Los Cazos)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"~35 m waterfall, ~45-min forest hike (or horseback) to a wooden overlook","bookable_category":"site entry (~US$1) + guide/horse","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.zonaturistica.com/en/things-to-do/jalisco/mazamitla/the-salto-waterfall (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"~35 m waterfall, ~45-min forest hike (or horseback) to a wooden overlook","commission":"day-tour or curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"La Zanja town forest","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"1977 municipal pine forest — trails, cabins, rentable grills","bookable_category":"free/low-cost","tier":"essential","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"1977 municipal pine forest — trails, cabins, rentable grills","commission":"curated-recommend","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Canopy + six hanging bridges (Green Forest Tours)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"future","hook":"3-hr zipline + 2-hr six-hanging-bridge forest walk","bookable_category":"operator","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","blurb":"3-hr zipline + 2-hr six-hanging-bridge forest walk","when":"year-round","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Chalet cabañas (Cabañas Monteverde)","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","hook":"Wooden chalet cabins with kitchens + fireplaces (daily firewood) — the definitive stay","bookable_category":"direct (domestic)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.travelagewest.com/Travel/Mexico/mazamitla-mexico-travel-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"family","blurb":"Wooden chalet cabins with kitchens + fireplaces (daily firewood) — the definitive stay","commission":"curated-recommend (direct-only)","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Enchanted Garden (Los Cazos)","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","hook":"Greenery + crystalline stream, toured on foot/bike/horseback/ATV","bookable_category":"site entry + rentals","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.travelagewest.com/Travel/Mexico/mazamitla-mexico-travel-guide (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"family","blurb":"Greenery + crystalline stream, toured on foot/bike/horseback/ATV","commission":"day-tour / curated","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Los Cazos ATV + horseback","si_tag":"Adventure / Ecotourism","status":"future","hook":"ATV tours + horse rides through pine-oak forest","bookable_category":"licensed operator","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theguadalajarapost.com/2022/06/03/mazamitla-jalisco-what-to-do-and-how-to-get-to-this-magical-town/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"Adventure / Ecotourism","blurb":"ATV tours + horse rides through pine-oak forest","commission":"activity affiliate / day-tour","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book a stay in Mazamitla through TravelWell?","a":"No — it is content-only, recommended only as a licensed day/weekend trip from the Guadalajara carve-out. Jalisco is US State Dept Level 3 (May 29, 2026) and Mazamitla is not one of the four named carve-outs; notably, though, the advisory names Mazamitla as an exception to the Highway 110 restriction and permits access \"via Highway 405 only.\" book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The ~2-hour mountain road transfer, not the town''s street crime (which is low — a domestic family town). The drive from Guadalajara leaves the GDL safe zone, even on the advisory-approved Highway 405, which is the hold reason; use licensed daytime transport only, and note the nearest full trauma hospital is ~2 hr back in Guadalajara.","source":"travel.state.gov / en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is there to do at El Salto waterfall?","a":"Hike to it. The ~35 m El Salto falls in Los Cazos are reached by a ~45-minute forest trail (or a horse, ~M$250) to a wooden overlook, entry ~US$1, with the fullest flow October–December after the rains. Sturdy footwear, and turn back in weather.","source":"zonaturistica.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Mazamitla good for a family weekend?","a":"Yes — it is the classic Guadalajara family escape. The product is a wooden chalet cabaña with a full kitchen and fireplace (Cabañas Monteverde delivers firewood daily) in a cool ~15°C pine-oak Pueblo Mágico at 2,200 m; cabañas sell out for Semana Santa, summer and Christmas, so book weeks to months ahead.","source":"travelagewest.com / en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"What adventure activities are on offer?","a":"Zip, ride and cross bridges. Green Forest Tours runs a 3-hour zipline and a 2-hour six-hanging-bridge walk, plus ATV, horseback and mountain-biking through the forest and Los Cazos. Use licensed operators with helmet/harness checks — evac to Guadalajara is ~2 hr, so injuries carry a distance penalty.","source":"theguadalajarapost.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"adventure"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mazamitla Travel Guide — Jalisco''s ''Mexican Switzerland'' Cabaña Mountain Pueblo Mágico | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Jalisco''s cool pine-forest Pueblo Mágico at 2,200 m — chalet cabañas, the El Salto waterfall, canopy tours, and straight guidance: a Level-3-interior day/weekend trip from Guadalajara (Hwy 405), not a bookable base.","slug":"mazamitla-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mazamitla Mexico travel guide","long_tail":["Mazamitla from Guadalajara day trip","El Salto waterfall Mazamitla","Mazamitla cabañas Monteverde","is Mazamitla safe","Mazamitla Suiza Mexicana things to do"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Mazamitla Pueblo Mágico","Mazamitla desde Guadalajara","cascada El Salto Mazamitla","cabañas en Mazamitla","Mazamitla la Suiza Mexicana","tirolesa puentes colgantes Mazamitla"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"future"},{"si":"family","status":"future"},{"si":"Adventure / Ecotourism","status":"future"}],"ultra":[],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Mazamitla, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.9153,"lng":-103.0208}}'::jsonb, 65),
  ('medellin-colombia', '10S', 'Medellín & Antioquia, Colombia', 'Colombia', 'Medellín & Antioquia', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Bogotá & The Andes', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["City of Eternal Spring — consistently mild climate year-round; elevation ~1,495 m","Comuna 13 is Medellín''s most-visited site; its 2011 outdoor escalators cut a 35-min climb to 6 min","El Peñol rock at Guatapé is climbed via 740 steps over an island-dotted reservoir, ~2 hrs east","Laureles named by Time Out one of the coolest neighborhoods in the world; El Poblado/Provenza is the polished tourist core","Feria de las Flores 2026 runs Jul 31–Aug 9, climaxing in the Aug 9 Desfile de Silleteros (530 silleteros)"],"safety":{"emergency":"123","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"dating_app_drugging_flag":true,"air_access_verified":"MDE / José María Córdova (Rionegro) — major direct-air gateway","altitude_m":1495,"notes":"Scopolamine/dating-app drugging — 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths in Medellín Nov–Dec 2023 (US Embassy). Trauma: medical-tourism hub w/ top private clinics; carry US-evac coverage. Dengue present. Tap water generally potable. Zone discipline: El Poblado/Laureles/Envigado; vetted transport; do not resist robbery."},"timing":{"peak":["December–March (drier)","July–August (drier)","Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 (headline peak)","December Alumbrados (secondary peak)"],"inflection":"Steep ramp from late June into the flower festival; December holidays/Alumbrados compress again","off_season_fill":["April–May","September–November"],"fire_date":"Feria de las Flores: fire by ~2026-07-15 (curve-start − 1–2 wks); December Alumbrados: fire late November"},"jewels":[{"name":"Comuna 13 graffiti + escalators (guided transformation tour)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Medellin/Guided-Tour-of-Comuna-13-Medellin-with-Snacks-Included/d4563-473336P1 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The city''s most-visited site; murals, escalators that cut a 35-min climb to 6, community art, street food","si":"culture","blurb":"The city''s most-visited site; murals, escalators that cut a 35-min climb to 6, community art, street food","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"non-commissionable / activity affiliate (vetted community operator)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Metrocable to Parque Arví","si_tag":"CHER/GEA","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.medellin.travel/what-to-do-in-medellin-neighborhoods-culture-and-creative-tourism/?lang=en (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Public gondola over the barrios up to a high cloud-forest ecological park — social urbanism and a jaw-dropping ride","si":"CHER/GEA","blurb":"Public gondola over the barrios up to a high cloud-forest ecological park — social urbanism and a jaw-dropping ride","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"non-commissionable transit anchoring paid Arví add-ons","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Botero Plaza + Museo de Antioquia","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/comuna-13-medellin-2026-street-art-transformation-tour.htm (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Downtown plaza of monumental Fernando Botero bronzes beside the region''s flagship art museum — pair with a morning Comuna 13 tour via the metro","si":"culture","blurb":"Downtown plaza of monumental Fernando Botero bronzes beside the region''s flagship art museum — pair with a morning Comuna 13 tour via the metro","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC-guided downtown add-on / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Guatapé + El Peñol rock (740 steps) + zócalos","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Medellin/Guatape-and-Penol-Rock-Full-Day-Tour/d4563-6033P27 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"~2 hrs east: climb the monolith over the island-studded reservoir, then wander Guatapé''s brightly painted zócalo streets and lakeside lunch","si":"expedition","blurb":"~2 hrs east: climb the monolith over the island-studded reservoir, then wander Guatapé''s brightly painted zócalo streets and lakeside lunch","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"day-trip operator affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Jardín & Jericó coffee pueblos + working-finca coffee tour","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Postcard Antioquian towns south of the city — plaza culture, cloud forest, and coffee at source with a finca tour/tasting","si":"expedition","blurb":"Postcard Antioquian towns south of the city — plaza culture, cloud forest, and coffee at source with a finca tour/tasting","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC / coffee-hacienda MoR stay","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Paragliding the Aburrá Valley (San Félix)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Tandem flight over the whole Medellín bowl — operator-vetted","si":"expedition","blurb":"Tandem flight over the whole Medellín bowl — operator-vetted","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC (operator-vetted only)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"El Poblado / Provenza & Manila dining","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"comfort","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Al-fresco brunches, world-class cocktail bars, Colombian tasting menus, Japanese-Colombian fusion, specialty coffee","si":"culinary","blurb":"Al-fresco brunches, world-class cocktail bars, Colombian tasting menus, Japanese-Colombian fusion, specialty coffee","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC dining add-ons / hotel F&B / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Feria de las Flores — silleteros (Jul 31–Aug 9, 2026)","si_tag":"RHN/CHER","tier":"comfort","source":"https://medellingroup.com/blog/feria-de-las-flores-2026-complete-guide-to-medellins-flower-festival (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The flower festival and its 530-silletero parade — the city''s headline peak; grandstand + curated hotel packages","si":"RHN/CHER","blurb":"The flower festival and its 530-silletero parade — the city''s headline peak; grandstand + curated hotel packages","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC festival packages + hotel/villa MoR","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Medellín a good place for a couples trip or honeymoon?","a":"Yes — for couples arriving together. El Poblado luxury apartments, rooftop-pool hotels and coffee-finca escapes are genuinely romantic. The plain caveat: the US Embassy links 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths in Medellín (Nov–Dec 2023) to dating-app-lured druggings, so the safe lane is partners who arrive together, not app meet-ups.","source":"co.usembassy.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is Comuna 13 and is it worth visiting?","a":"Yes — Comuna 13 is Medellín''s most-visited site and the emblem of its turnaround. Outdoor public escalators installed in 2011 cut a 35-minute climb to 6 minutes; today the hillside barrio is a canvas of community murals, told on a guided walking tour (~$20–30). Go guided, daytime, as a group.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do you visit Guatapé and El Peñol rock from Medellín?","a":"Guatapé sits about 2 hours east, usually as a full-day trip. The headline is climbing El Peñol (Piedra del Peñol) via 740 steps — most reach the top in 15–25 minutes — over a reservoir dotted with islands, then wandering the brightly painted zócalo streets. Book a day-trip operator or DMC.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Medellín?","a":"The signature Medellín danger is dating-app drugging-and-robbery, not the headlines. The US Embassy is aware of 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths (Nov 1–Dec 31, 2023) involving scopolamine (\"burundanga\") — odorless, memory-erasing and lethal in large doses. Don''t meet app strangers alone, never leave a drink unattended, and meet only in public.","source":"co.usembassy.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is climbing El Peñol''s 740 steps dangerous?","a":"It''s a steep but manageable self-guided climb — 740 steps, 15–25 minutes for most — though not for those with cardiac or mobility limits. Pace it, hydrate, and mind your footing on the descent. Paragliding over the Aburrá Valley, by contrast, should be flown only with certified, insured, safety-vetted operators.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Medellín & Antioquia Travel Guide 2026 — Comuna 13, Guatapé, Coffee Country | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-CO","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Medellín","Comuna 13 tour","Guatapé Peñol","Feria de las Flores","dónde hospedarse en Medellín","seguridad Medellín aplicaciones de citas"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"],"freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Medellín & Antioquia"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"The Charlee","location":"El Poblado","note":"Envy rooftop pool/bar, 360° valley views; most-photographed hotel in Colombia","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Diez Hotel Categoría Colombia","location":"El Poblado","note":"Colombian-art boutique, full-service spa","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"The Click Clack Hotel Medellín","location":"El Poblado","note":"Design-forward, artisan interiors, rooftop; Mr & Mrs Smith listed","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"Luxury coffee-country haciendas (Hacienda Bambusa / Sazagua-tier)","location":"Antioquia / Coffee-Triangle-adjacent","note":"Rural ultra pairing","program":"MoR","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"NOTE — Four Seasons Casa Medina","location":"Bogotá (NOT Medellín)","note":"Do not misassign to Medellín","program":"n/a","price_tier":"$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Medellín & Antioquia, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":6.2442,"lng":-75.5812}}'::jsonb, 66),
