lunch (Zuccardi Piedra Infinita, Salentein + Kilka)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.mrwinery.com/tour/visit-zuccardi-piedra-infinita-and-have-lunch-at-bodega","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%"},{"name":"The Vines estate tasting + vine-side table","si_tag":"culinary+romance","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.scottdunn.com/us/argentina/hotels/the-vines-resort-spa","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the resort''s own vineyard program and vine-side dining, a natural CUL+RHM crossover","si":"culinary+romance","blurb":"the resort''s own vineyard program and vine-side dining, a natural CUL+RHM crossover","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"DMC / lodge package 10–20%"},{"name":"Luján de Cuyo classic Malbec cellars","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/lujan-de-cuyo-from-mendoza-wine-route-2026-malbec-guide.htm","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the historic, powerful, ripe Luján style; best infrastructure + easiest access from the city","si":"culinary","blurb":"the historic, powerful, ripe Luján style; best infrastructure + easiest access from the city","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Catena Zapata pyramid + Blending Games","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Mendoza/Catena-Zapata-Wine-Tour-from-Mendoza/d931-5693P18","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","si":"culinary","blurb":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"private-transport DMC/affiliate 4–20%"},{"name":"Maipú bike-and-wine + olive-oil & asado","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-travel-guide-2026-argentinas-wine-capital.htm","hook":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","si":"culinary","blurb":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Achaval-Ferrer single-vineyard Malbec","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-wine-tours-2026-best-wineries-tastings.htm","si":"culinary","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Sunrise hot-air balloon over the vineyards","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/argentina-l168992/hot-air-balloon-ride-over-mendoza-s-vineyards-wine-toast-t876044/","hook":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","si":"romance","blurb":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","commission":"affiliate 4–8% / DMC bundle"},{"name":"Cacheuta thermal springs","si_tag":"romance+wellness","tier":"comfort","source":"https://thewholeworldornothing.com/hot-springs-mendoza-cacheuta-thermal-baths/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","si":"romance+wellness","blurb":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate spa day 4–8% / DMC"},{"name":"Alta Montaña + Aconcagua viewpoint + Puente del Inca","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/mendoza-l673/andes-day-trip-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-t55889/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","si":"expedition","blurb":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / affiliate day 4–20%"},{"name":"Mendoza River rafting (Potrerillos)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/adventure-tourism-in-potrerillos-mendoza/","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Uspallata & the high desert","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.myguideargentina.com/experiences/mendoza-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-day-trip","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","si":"expedition","blurb":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC day 10–20%"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mendoza the world''s Malbec capital?","a":"Because the concentration is unmatched: Argentina holds roughly 75% of the world''s Malbec vines, and about 75% of Argentina''s vineyards lie in Mendoza — making it the single most important place on the planet for the grape and the global epicenter of Malbec.","source":"winefolly.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mendoza?","a":"Late February through April — harvest and the Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia (2026 central acts Mar 6–10) — is the most atmospheric window. Spring (Oct–Nov) is the value-and-balance alternative, with rates running ~15–25% below harvest peaks; either way, book icon wineries and lodges 3–4 months ahead of the Feb–April peak.","source":"across-southamerica.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Which honeymoon wine-lodge should we book?","a":"The two ultra beds are Awasi Mendoza (Relais & Châteaux, Luján de Cuyo, 18 adobe rooms/villas on a ~60-acre private vineyard) and The Vines Resort & Spa (Valle de Uco, 21 private villas across 1,500 acres with vine-side dining). Both commission best through luxury consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), typically ~10%+ plus amenities.","source":"scottdunn.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you see Aconcagua on a day trip from Mendoza?","a":"Yes. Route 7 climbs the Alta Montaña corridor past Potrerillos (1,350 m), Uspallata (1,900 m), and Puente del Inca (2,720 m) to the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak, the highest in the Western Hemisphere. The day-trip tops out ~2,700 m (mild breathlessness possible); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is a separate, expedition-grade activity requiring permits and licensed guides.","source":"getyourguide.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mendoza?","a":"Drink-driving. Wine touring plus self-drive is the single most important avoidable risk, so the standard doctrine is always a designated driver or a guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings, and ride sober on the Maipú bike-and-wine route.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mendoza River rafting dangerous?","a":"Guided, it is a managed risk. Rafting at Potrerillos runs Class II–III, up to Class IV in high summer flow, with certified rescue guides, kayak safety support, and full neoprene/helmet/PFD standard — book certified operators only, and never run the river unguided.","source":"solsalute.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mendoza & Argentina Wine Country — Malbec, Valle de Uco & the Andes | TravelWell","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["bodegas Mendoza","Valle de Uco vinos","Ruta del Vino Mendoza","Vendimia","Alta Montaña Aconcagua","termas de Cacheuta","Malbec de altura"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Mendoza (formerly Cavas Wine Lodge)","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"18 adobe rooms/villas on ~60-acre private vineyard","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"The Vines Resort & Spa","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"21 private vineyard villas on 1,500 acres + spa + vine-side dining","earning":"consortia commission + villa MoR","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa de Uco","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"modern estate rooms, pool + spa, working-vineyard finca","earning":"consortia / DMC commission","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Entre Cielos","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"design hotel in 3.2 ha Malbec vines + Hammam spa circuit","earning":"consortia / bedbank premium","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-32.8895,"lng":-68.8458}}'::jsonb, 67)
