e northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry; overlaps humpback season Dec–Mar)","shoulder":"May–Jun, late Oct","green":"Jul–Oct (rainy/hurricane season)","booking_lead":"Dec–Mar villas 4–6+ months; shoulder 6–10 weeks","off_season_specials":"Jul–Oct value campaign: beaches + diving + villa-with-chef (no whales)","event_peaks":"US/Canada winter holidays (late Dec–early Jan); spring break (Mar)","campaign_start":"Aug–Sep for whale/Romance (Dec–Mar arrivals); May–Jun for green-season value"},"jewels":[{"name":"Humpback panga at dawn, Banderas Bay","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"~500–700 humpbacks breed within sight of shore Dec–Mar","bookable_category":"tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://mismaloyaxtreme.com/en/whale-watching-puerto-vallarta-2025-2026-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"~500–700 humpbacks breed within sight of shore Dec–Mar","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC/tour affiliate ~8–15%","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Los Arcos National Park dive","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Deepest water in the bay — tunnels, rays, turtles","bookable_category":"tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.vallarta-adventures.com/en/tour/scuba-los-arcos (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Deepest water in the bay — tunnels, rays, turtles","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"tour affiliate ~8–12%","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Marietas Islands","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Pacific mantas + reef fish + Hidden Beach","bookable_category":"tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.vallarta-adventures.com/en/tour/scuba-las-marietas-islands (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"Pacific mantas + reef fish + Hidden Beach","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"tour affiliate ~8–12%","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Casa Kimberly","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"The Taylor/Burton love-story hotel, heart-shaped-tub suite","bookable_category":"hotel","tier":"luxury","source":"https://travellemming.com/hotels-in-puerto-vallarta/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"The Taylor/Burton love-story hotel, heart-shaped-tub suite","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"hotel/host commission ~10%","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Conchas Chinas villa with private chef","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Hillside beachfront villa, chef/butler, minutes from Romantic Zone","bookable_category":"villa","tier":"luxury","source":"https://villaexperience.com/city/puerto-vallarta/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Hillside beachfront villa, chef/butler, minutes from Romantic Zone","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"villa-agency commission via host (MoR ~10%)","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Staying in the tourist zone, not the interior. Fly into PVR (no need to transit the restricted interior), remain within PV / the Banderas Bay resort corridor, and don''t self-drive into the Jalisco interior. Health-wise, dengue is seasonal in the Jul–Oct rains — use repellent — and there is no malaria in the resort zone.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When and how can I see the whales?","a":"On a licensed panga, roughly Dec 8–Mar 23, best in the morning. Around 500–700 humpbacks arrive in Banderas Bay each winter to breed and calve within sight of shore; whales are federally protected, so keep the regulated distance and do not swim with them. Morning departures mean calmer seas.","source":"mismaloyaxtreme.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Puerto Vallarta good for a honeymoon, and where''s the top end?","a":"Yes — it''s a mature honeymoon and destination-wedding market. The in-city ultra rung is narrow but real: Hotel Mousai is PV''s only AAA Five-Diamond (145 suites + 4 penthouses), and the 9-room Casa Kimberly is the Taylor/Burton love-story hotel. Peak is Nov–Apr; hold marquee rooms and villas early.","source":"travellemming.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can beginners dive Los Arcos?","a":"Los Arcos is a certified-diver site, not a beginner pool — it holds the deepest water in Banderas Bay, with tunnels, arches, rays and turtles. Dive within your certification, and observe the DAN no-fly interval of 18–24 hours before boarding a flight from PVR. Marietas Islands is the other certified-reef option.","source":"vallarta-adventures.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean-adventures-—-future"},{"q":"Where are the best villas?","a":"Conchas Chinas and Amapas. PV''s \"Beverly Hills\" hillside enclave holds beachfront estates with private chef and butler just 5–10 minutes from the Romantic Zone; book Dec–Mar (the whale-and-holiday peak) 4–6+ months ahead. Route villas as agency/host merchant-of-record, never net-rate resale.","source":"casabayvillas.com / villaexperience.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Puerto Vallarta Travel Guide 2026 — Whales, Villas & Banderas Bay | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Puerto Vallarta: humpback whale season (Dec–Mar), luxury villas in Conchas Chinas, Five-Diamond resorts, and diving Los Arcos — with the Jalisco Level 3 advisory explained and PV''s named carve-out.","primary_keywords":["Puerto Vallarta travel","Puerto Vallarta whale watching","Puerto Vallarta luxury villas","is Puerto Vallarta safe 2026"],"long_tail":["Puerto Vallarta humpback whale season dates","Conchas Chinas villa rental with chef","Puerto Vallarta Level 3 advisory carve-out","diving Los Arcos Puerto Vallarta"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["avistamiento de ballenas Puerto Vallarta","villas de lujo Conchas Chinas","Puerto Vallarta es seguro 2026","buceo Los Arcos Puerto Vallarta","hoteles todo incluido Puerto Vallarta"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Mousai","why_ultra":"Only AAA Five-Diamond resort in PV; hilltop suites + penthouses over Banderas Bay","earning":"on application / via host","virtuoso_value_add":"verify Virtuoso/preferred; if listed, breakfast + credit + upgrade","mor":"hotel"},{"name":"Garza Blanca Preserve Resort & Spa","why_ultra":"Private-beach sister to Mousai; shared facilities","earning":"on application / via host","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":"hotel"},{"name":"Casa Kimberly","why_ultra":"9-room Taylor/Burton icon, bay-view Taylor suite","earning":"host/hotel commission on application","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":"hotel"},{"name":"Conchas Chinas / Amapas luxury villas (e.g. Villa Amapas South)","why_ultra":"~7,000 sq ft beachfront estate, chef/butler","earning":"villa-agency commission via host, on application","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a (villa)","mor":"agency/host (never net-rate resale)"},{"name":"One&Only Mandarina [Nayarit — state-line flag]","why_ultra":"Ultra resort in neighboring Riviera Nayarit, inside PV safety carve-out","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":"hotel"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Puerto Vallarta, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.6534,"lng":-105.2253}}'::jsonb, 85)
